# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Ignore rules
#
#  Principle: anything that should not be visible to the whole world must
#  never enter the git history. History is permanent — deleting a file in a
#  later commit does not remove it from earlier ones. Over-blocking is cheap;
#  under-blocking is not recoverable without rewriting history.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
dist/
.astro/

# ── Dependencies ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/

# ── Logs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# ── Secrets: keys, tokens, credentials ───────────────────────────────────
# These belong in the hosting provider's environment variables, never in
# the repository.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.dev.vars
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials.json
secrets.json

# ── Internal business and legal documents ────────────────────────────────
# Incorporation paperwork, financial planning, and contracts stay in the
# organization's own document storage. The rules below are a safety net
# against an accidental drag-and-drop into the project folder.
/private/
/docs-internal/
*.doc
*.docx
*.xls
*.xlsx
*.ppt
*.pptx
*.pdf
# Exception: PDFs under public/ are deliberately published for visitors to
# download, such as tournament rules and entry forms.
!public/**/*.pdf

# ── Editor and OS files ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
*.swp
*~
